{"id":73,"frontend_id":73,"title":"Maximum Unique Subarray","slug":"maximum-unique-subarray","difficulty":"Medium","pattern_category":"arrays","tags":["arrays","dataset"],"company_tags":["Adobe"],"ac_rate":"49.9%","statement":"# Maximum Sum of Distinct Subarray\nYou are given an array of positive integers `nums`. Return the maximum possible sum of a contiguous subarray of `nums` such that all the values in the subarray are distinct. If no such subarray exists, return 0.\n\n### Examples\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** `nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]`\n\n**Output:** `15`\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** `nums = [1, 1, 1, 1, 1]`\n\n**Output:** `1`\n","hints":[],"starter_code_python":"class Solution:\n    def solve(self, nums: list) -> int:\n        max_sum = 0\n        for i in range(len(nums)):\n            distinct_nums = set()\n            current_sum = 0\n            for j in range(i, len(nums)):\n                if nums[j] not in distinct_nums:\n                    distinct_nums.add(nums[j])\n                    current_sum += nums[j]\n                    max_sum = max(max_sum, current_sum)\n                else:\n                    break\n        return max_sum","example_test_cases":[{"stdin":"{\"nums\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]}","expected_stdout":"15","is_hidden":false,"order":0},{"stdin":"{\"nums\": [1, 1, 1, 1, 1]}","expected_stdout":"1","is_hidden":false,"order":1}],"hidden_test_cases":[{"stdin":"{\"nums\": [5, 1, 1, 5]}","expected_stdout":"6","is_hidden":true,"order":2},{"stdin":"{\"nums\": [1, 2, 3, 2, 1]}","expected_stdout":"6","is_hidden":true,"order":3},{"stdin":"{\"nums\": [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60]}","expected_stdout":"210","is_hidden":true,"order":4},{"stdin":"{\"nums\": [5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 1]}","expected_stdout":"6","is_hidden":true,"order":5},{"stdin":"{\"nums\": []}","expected_stdout":"0","is_hidden":true,"order":6},{"stdin":"{\"nums\": [1]}","expected_stdout":"1","is_hidden":true,"order":7},{"stdin":"{\"nums\": [7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7]}","expected_stdout":"7","is_hidden":